From 4fd5cf42270419ca89039e392bba479aecf85145 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel JB Clark <djbclark@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 06:27:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Tightened JsonParseStrict to reject remaining non-RFC-8259
 forms

Reject leading/trailing commas, missing array commas, raw control
characters (0x01-0x1f), unrecognized or malformed escapes and unpaired
UTF-16 surrogates, leading zeros after unary minus (-00/-01), decimal
points after exponents (1e2.3), and objects exceeding 65536 members in
JsonParseStrict(). Salt the strict duplicate-key hash set seed and make
boolean/null literal prefix matching O(1) via strncmp() instead of
StringStartsWith() to avoid quadratic strlen scans, while preserving
lenient JsonParse().

Changelog: Title
Ticket: none
Signed-off-by: Daniel JB Clark <djbclark@gmail.com>
